CORE
main.c
--verbosity 10
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
line 10 dereference failure: pointer outside object bounds in \*i.*: FAILURE
line 13 dereference failure: pointer outside object bounds in \(&a\).*: FAILURE
--
--
The line 14 dereference of `i` is the same out-of-bounds access as the one at
line 10; goto_check_c deduplicates the repeated check against the line 10 one
on some platforms (e.g. Visual Studio), so it is not pinned here. The line 10
failure and the overall VERIFICATION FAILED still cover it.
